      "detail": "8th in Atlantic Division",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The season didn't just drift off the ice; it crashed through the boards - and now Toronto is left staring at a <strong>32-36-14</strong> record, <strong>8th in the Atlantic Division</strong>, <strong>78 points</strong>, and a <strong>15th</strong>-place playoff seed, a finish that says underachievement in bold type. <strong>Bourne's case for Gavin McKenna at No. 1</strong> has quickly become the loudest draft storyline around the club, and it fits a team that needs more than a tweak; it needs a jolt. The Maple Leafs spent the year bleeding points and never found a true answer in the middle of the lineup, while the season-ending <strong>L7</strong> underscored how quickly the bottom fell out. The bigger question now is who steers the repair job - the coaching search, the free-agent board, and the draft table all matter, but they matter in that order because Toronto can't afford another soft reset disguised as continuity. The next move has to be decisive, not decorative, because a proud franchise with 78 points and no runway left has earned only one luxury: honesty. <strong>Watch the coaching decision and the push toward draft night - that is where Toronto's next season begins.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated June 11, 2026"
      },
