        "label": "What's Going On With the Commanders",
        "body": "A quiet spring can still hide a hard truth: the roster is already asking its first brutal questions. <strong>The loudest current thread is the fight for roles at receiver and in the secondary, with Luke McCaffrey and UDFA Jaden Bradley both pulling attention while Mikey Sainristil looks like a defender on the rise.</strong> Washington sits 3rd in the NFC East, 6 games back, with a 3-0? no - the verified numbers say 3rd place, a W1 streak, and the kind of shallow footing that makes every OTA rep matter even if the standings only tell part of the story. The Commanders are in minicamp now, and that means the real work is less about headlines than about sorting the depth chart: who can separate, who can learn fast, who can survive the new scheme without blinking. McCaffrey was once easy to forget; now he is forcing his way back into the conversation. Sainristil, meanwhile, is becoming the type of young piece coaches trust because he shows up where the ball does. <strong>Watch the next wave of camp practices - that is where the receiver pecking order and the defensive back rotation will start to harden.</strong>",
